  "goodToKnow": "Die Bundesebene is the federal level, as opposed to die Landesebene (state level) and die kommunale Ebene (municipal level). Germany's federalism splits responsibilities: defence and foreign policy are on Bundesebene, schools and police mainly on Landesebene. Parties often govern in different coalitions auf Bundes- und Landesebene. Die Ebene also means a plain (landscape). It has no plural."
